{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1302487-stv-paris-changeling-city-or-crossover-city","id":1302487,"title":"[STV] Paris-Changeling City or Crossover City?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-04T00:11:04-07:00","id":1302487,"title":"[STV] Paris-Changeling City or Crossover City?","content":"Hey kids, it's been a bit. Let's talk Paris.<br /> <br /> For those of you who are new to the discussion, a quick primer: I was a writer for the first rendition of Changeling the Lost Second Edition, and my section was a freehold for the city of Paris called <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-3ZZ_vJMgEhWG5uQkJjczFaZ1E/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Rosiere</a>* (missing accents because keeping it easy), a city of romance, duels, and theatrics on the surface hiding a system of sacrifice, manipulation, and role confinement that began to rival the True Fae, all wrapped up in the City of Lights. Due to some misgivings about that transition (no conversation on that in this thread, please, thank you), I opted to instead release an updated version of The Rosiere as a fan release and waited for Second Edition to come out proper. Annnnd it's been some time since then.<br /> <br /> By and large, this is because my last year and a half have been....busy, but a large part of that is also that the game has <i>changed</i> since then, and not just with the proper Second Edition(no problems with that, for the record). Clearly I've opened up to OP again, and I'm open to The Rosiere being canon material, but the plan still goes forward with it as fan material. There's some things, like Entitlements, that I'm still waiting on before I try and do the Rosiere right, but the main things were the introduction of the Storyteller's Vault and the general push towards crossover starting with Dark Eras and culminating in Contagion now. The main reason for that factoring in now is that Paris....originally was not a Changeling centric setting for me.<br /> <br /> The first time I ever put the name Paris into text for Chronicles games actually stemmed from a desire to run a crossover game where in the player group would seek out a 5 Dot Seba about to arrive in order to facilitate a Deceived's attempt to achieve Apotheosis, and thereby set a regular character in my games from then on, at least in a different way from the way I normally do it. Since then, a lot of conversations with fellows writers and gamers has emphasized how crossover is a underutilized strength of Chronicles, and with the release of Geist and other materials being out, thinking about Paris has become something of a swim around various incarnations of how Paris as a crossover city might manifest.<br /> <br /> At this point, The Rosiere as it exists is...not going to matter so much to me personally in terms of the games I'm going to be running from here on out. So as such, the final form of Paris ultimately matters more to you all, so I decided to pitch it to you all to see how we should go forward. I've got four options here to look at, though I'm open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> 1) The Rosiere Alone: Basically, we keep the status quo-The Rosiere comes up to date with more support(Contracts, Crowns, better Mantles, etc.)<br /> <br /> 2) The Rosiere Among The Houses: The Rosiere as part of a larger look into Paris demonstrating each of the gamelines in isolation from one another. You might get cheeky references to one another across the stuff, but it's not quite <i>crossover</i> crossover.<br /> <br /> 3) The Rosiere In The Woods: The Rosiere is a crossover faction, one of many in Paris, and it's not the only one that changelings join-some may align with beasts and werewolves, some with mummies and Sin-Eaters. Holy orders of demons and Sin-Eaters seek to create the Throne of God, Libertines and wolf children alike dash the pillars of euros, and more are the sort of stuff you'd see here.<br /> <br /> 4) The Rosiere Upon The Throne: The Rosiere is a crossover faction, and it rules over all the monsters. Mages and demons debate across the lines of the Blue and Gold Roses about reality, while Prometheans and vampires flirt across all dualities as members of the Red and White Roses, that sort of thing. They may also double as Contagion-based factions, though Paris will not be presented under the context of a current Contagion outbreak.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm open to options. I'm not quite opening the door since I'm currently kicking The Noble and The Sovereign and seeing what needs placement before going public with that, so it's still gonna be some bit before I get to the Rosiere proper, which works out since I'm still waiting on other materials (namely the Changeling Companion).<br /> <br /> And as an aside, if any of you have anything you'd like to see me throw a hand at for STV material, this is also a good time to let me know. I doubt I'll do anything as big as the Rosiere project, but if you've ever wanted to see me make some Werewolf or Beast or Hunter or whatever material and don't feel like waiting for me to grab contracts, let me know.<br /> <br /> *And for those of you wondering about the Sleeping Lions and the Forest of Teeth-don't worry, we've still got eyes on that fam, just need this answered first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"}